d\n\nAdding the contributions (2) and (5) and substituting \\(r=n-k\\),\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\bigl|\\bigcup_{b=1}^{r}L_{b}\\bigr|+|T|\n&= rn-\\frac{r(r-1)}{2}+\\frac{k(k+1)}{2}\\\\\n&= (n-k)n-\\frac{(n-k)(n-k-1)}{2}+\\frac{k(k+1)}{2}\\\\\n&= \\frac{n(n+1)}{2}=|S|.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nThus condition (A) holds, and exactly \\(k\\) of the \\(n\\) lines (the\n\\(\\ell_{i}\\)’s) are sunny.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 3. Completeness of the range of \\(k\\)\n\nThe construction works for every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\):\n\n* **\\(k=0\\).**  Take the \\(n\\) horizontal lines \\(y=1,\\dots ,y=n\\) (all\n  non‑sunny).\n* **\\(k=n\\).**  Take the \\(n\\) sunny lines \\(\\ell_{i}\\) with\n  \\(d_{i}=i-1\\) (no horizontal line is needed).\n* **\\(0<k<n\\).**  Use the construction described in Sections 2.1–2.3.\n\nTogether with the bound (1), no other values of \\(k\\) are possible.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0\\le k\\le n}.\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
